      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_463",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:play_music",
            file: "main_menu.ogg",
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("In the twenty-eighth year of the reign of Garard II, King of Wesnoth, the kingdom made bitter war against the Orcs of the North."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_464",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("The Northern host encamped at Galcadar, by the Ford of Abez, and the King led his forces to meet them. Years of war brought Wesnoth to the brink of ruin, but at long last victory was won through the actions of Garard’s arch-mage, Delfador."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_465",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("story/httt_story1.webp"),
            text: _("Garard’s son, the Crown Prince Eldred, joined in the revelry as the King celebrated his victory. Eldred was bright and driven, and might one day have grown into a wise ruler. Unfortunately for Garard, his son was also ambitious... and treacherous."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_466",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("story/httt_story2.webp"),
            text: _("At the height of Garard’s triumph, Eldred struck the old King down in cold blood. Seizing the crown for himself, the young prince led his father’s army south towards Weldyn."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_467",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("story/httt_story3.webp"),
            text: _("Garard’s queen, Asheviere, looked on with glee, having orchestrated much of her son’s treachery. The rule of Eldred would surely satisfy her lust for power far better than her husband’s had."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_468",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("story/httt_story4.webp"),
            text: _("But Delfador the arch-mage had not fallen alongside his king. Returning from a distant battle, he mustered a force of loyalists to fight the young prince and avenge the King’s death. The loyalist army marched south to meet Eldred."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_469",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Eldred made war upon the loyalists with his mother’s advice ringing in his ears: <i>“Fight no one great or small except the old mage, whose head should be severed from his shoulders.”</i>"),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_470",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("story/httt_story5.webp"),
            text: _("And Eldred did indeed meet Delfador face-to-face in battle, along the high road to Weldyn. Sword clashed against staff, as the wise old mage fought the brash young warrior."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_471",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("story/httt_story6.webp"),
            text: _("In the end Delfador’s men were defeated and routed, but Asheviere found her son’s lifeless body, fixed to the ground by the great mage’s staff."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_472",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Asheviere herself then took command of the army and led it back to Weldyn. Knowing that the King’s young nephews were next in line to the throne, she ordered them all killed and declared herself Queen of Wesnoth, striking down any lord bold enough to oppose her."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_473",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("story/httt_story7.webp"),
            text: _("Soon after news of Asheviere’s orders reached Delfador, he secretly entered the palace and stole away Konrad, the youngest of Garard’s nephews, thereby saving him from death."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_474",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("story/httt_story8.webp~FL()"),
            text: _("Fleeing to the Aethenwood beyond the south-western border of Wesnoth, Delfador raised the child Konrad under the protection of the elves, watching sadly as Asheviere’s reign of terror over the land began..."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "loyal_475",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:make_loyal",
            units: "Konrad,redmage,leader4,leader5,leader6,Konrad,Konrad",
          },
        ],
      },
